<p>This system is designed to provide more information about each of the 
 printer features supported by the RPCS printer driver.</p>
<h2>Displaying Help for the Printer Driver</h2>
<ul>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Help</span> button 
 in the dialog box to display an explanation of the dialog box. Click the 
 <span class="Term-OS">Contents</span> tab in the left window to display 
 the table of contents. From here you can view each Help topic.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the item whose Help topics you want to 
 see, and then press the <span class="Term-Hard">F1</span> key.</p></li>
<li><p>If a question mark button is displayed in the 
 upper right corner of the printing preferences dialog box, click it. Your 
 mouse's pointer will change to a question mark <img alt="" class="help-icon" height="20" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/IcHelp.gif" width="23"/>. Move this 
 question mark over the item whose Help information you want to view, and 
 then left-click to display the Help information.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2>Printing Help Topics</h2>
<ul>
<li><p>To print the currently displayed <span class="Term-Soft">Help</span> 
 topic, click the <span class="Term-OS">Print</span> button at the top.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2>Note for Printer Driver Tabs and Dialog Boxes</h2>
<ul>
<li><p>The <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> and 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> tabs are not available in 
 the printing preferences dialog box when accessing from the application's 
 <span class="Term-OS">Print</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>When you make settings on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 and <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> tabs, you must log on 
 as a member of the Administrators or Power Users group.</p></li>
</ul>
